  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $4$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nIf $h(x)=(-2f(x)-3)(g(x)+1),$ find the value of ${h}^{′}(2).$\n\n${h}^{′}(2)=$\n{{field-1}}",
